Every Arduino sketch is built around two fundamental functions:

```cpp
void setup() {
  // Hardware configuration — runs ONCE at boot or reset
  pinMode(13, OUTPUT);
}

void loop() {
  // Perpetual cycle — runs REPEATEDLY forever
  digitalWrite(13, HIGH);
  delay(1000);
  digitalWrite(13, LOW);
  delay(1000);
}
```

- `setup()`: Initializes GPIO pin directions and communications. It runs exactly once when power is applied.
- `loop()`: The infinite heartbeat of your robot. Once `setup()` finishes, the microcontroller jumps into `loop()` and orbits perpetually.

Run the interactive lifecycle simulator below to watch `setup()` illuminate its beacon once, followed by the continuous orbit of `loop()`!
